#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# set_attributes

#% text
# `set_attributes(f, a)` gives the symbol `f` the attribute `a`; `set_attributes(f, [a, b, ...])` several.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `listable`: calls with list arguments map over them; `hold_all`, `hold_first`, `hold_rest`: arguments are passed unevaluated; `orderless`: an associative and commutative head; `flat`: an associative head (nested calls are spliced in, the order is kept, and a pattern argument may match a run of arguments wrapped in the head); `effect`: calls perform effects; `handles_failures`: failures arrive as arguments.

#% item
# `protected`: the symbol's definitions may not change (see `protect`). `locked`, `read_protected`, `numeric_function`, `one_identity` and `constant` are accepted and change nothing.

#% item
# The attributes of a protected symbol change only by removing `protected`; otherwise the value is `failure(protected, f)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
set_attributes(f1, listable)
f1([1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [f1(1), f1(2), f1(3)]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Held arguments:

#% cell
set_attributes(q1, hold_all)
q1(1 + 1)
#% output
#= q1(1 + 1)

#% text
# `flat` splices nested calls, also in an `orderless` head, which sorts them:

#% cell
set_attributes(ff, flat)
set_attributes(oo, [orderless, flat])
[ff(ff(1, 2), ff(3, 4)), oo(oo(c, a), b)]
#% output
#= [ff(1, 2, 3, 4), oo(a, b, c)]

#% text
# Several symbols at once, and the held arguments of `hold_first` and `hold_rest`:

#% cell
set_attributes([p1, p2], listable)
set_attributes(h1, hold_first)
set_attributes(h2, hold_rest)
[attributes(p1), attributes(p2), h1(1 + 1, 2 + 2), h2(1 + 1, 2 + 2)]
#% output
#= [[listable], [listable], h1(1 + 1, 4), h2(2, 2 + 2)]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `clear_attributes` undoes it:

#% cell
set_attributes(f2, listable)
clear_attributes(f2, listable)
f2([1, 2])
#% output
#= f2([1, 2])

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# An unknown attribute and a name that is not a symbol are failures:

#% cell
[set_attributes(zz, foo), set_attributes(2, listable)]
#% output
#= [failure(argument, set_attributes, 2), failure(argument, set_attributes, 1)]

#% text
# The attributes that are accepted and change nothing are not stored:

#% cell
set_attributes(pp, [flat, one_identity])
attributes(pp)
#% output
#= [flat]

#% text
# A rule on a flat head sees the whole run of arguments:

#% cell
set_attributes(g1, flat)
rule g1(x_, y_) := x + y
g1(1, 2, 3)
#% output
#= 6

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `attributes`, `clear_attributes`, `map`
